<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baikonur Cosmodrome</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Baikonur Cosmodrome is a space launch site on the steppe of southern Kazakhstan, near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syr-darya">Syr Darya</a>. Built by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> from 1955, it launched <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sputnik-1">Sputnik 1</a> in 1957 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuri-gagarin">Yuri Gagarin</a>, the first man in space, in 1961. Since 1991 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> has leased it from Kazakhstan and continues to use it for crewed flights.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baikonur-cosmodrome.jpg" alt="Baikonur Cosmodrome" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bill Ingalls · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Baikonur_Cosmodrome_Soyuz_launch_pad.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
